/**
 * One-off script: Phase 4 Location & Address Architecture — seeds
 * `neighborhoods/{neighborhoodId}` from the validated OCHA COD-AB-SYR
 * `syr_neighborhoods` extraction (see the Phase 2 data-acquisition report
 * and the Phase 3 validation report — 414 records across Damascus, Aleppo,
 * Homs, Lattakia, Tartous, Ar-Raqqa, Hama, Deir-ez-Zor, Al-Hasakeh, Dar'a,
 * Idleb, As-Sweida, and the Yarmuk special case). Every nameEn/nameAr value
 * below is copied verbatim from that extraction — nothing invented,
 * reconstructed from memory, or auto-translated — with exactly two
 * source-data handling decisions, both already reported in Phase 3:
 *
 *  1. Aleppo N0164 ("Ad-Dallain") — OCHA's own source file stores the
 *     Arabic name tripled with embedded line breaks (a confirmed data-entry
 *     artifact, verified directly in the raw XLSX sharedStrings.xml).
 *     Stored once here — "الدلالين" — per Phase 4 requirement #4.
 *  2. Yarmuk (N0109-N0111) — OCHA's own P-code hierarchy scopes these three
 *     records under a distinct adm4 locality ("Yarmuk"/اليرموك, pcode
 *     C1002), structurally parallel to Damascus city itself (pcode C1001)
 *     rather than nested inside it. Seeded under cityId "damascus_yarmuk"
 *     (see seed-syrian-cities-phase4.ts, which must run first) rather than
 *     folded into Damascus's other 97 neighbourhoods, per Phase 4
 *     requirement #5.
 *
 * enabled:false marks the four records the Phase 3 validation report
 * classified as SPECIAL_AREA/INDUSTRIAL_AREA/CAMP (a university campus, two
 * industrial zones, one refugee camp) — kept in the dataset (never
 * deleted), just excluded from the customer-facing neighbourhood picker via
 * NeighborhoodOption.enabled, same mechanism models/neighborhood.dart's own
 * doc comment describes. Every other record is enabled:true, INCLUDING the
 * Phase 3 REQUIRES_REVIEW records (ambiguous "_"/"/"-joined compound names,
 * and Dar'a's neighbourhood literally named "Quneitra") — those are real,
 * selectable places flagged for a future manual naming review, not
 * unsuitable for the picker; see the Phase 3 report's Section 2 for the
 * full reasoning per record.
 *
 * [id] is a proposed slug (`<cityId>_<normalized_english_name>`, with the
 * source P-code appended on a same-city collision) — the same scheme
 * proposed as a CANDIDATE in the Phase 2 report, now finalized as the
 * actual document id. [ochaPcode] preserves the traceability link back to
 * the exact OCHA source row.
 *
 * Requires seed-syrian-cities-phase4.ts (and the original seed-cities.ts)
 * to have already run — firestore.rules' neighborhoods/{neighborhoodId}
 * create rule requires the referenced cities/{cityId} doc to exist.
 *
 * Writes via the Admin SDK, bypassing firestore.rules — same as every
 * other seed script in this directory. Every doc id is deterministic and
 * written with `.set()`, so re-running this script is a safe, idempotent
 * overwrite.
 *
 * Usage (real project):
 *   GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS="$env:APPDATA\firebase\<you>_application_default_credentials.json" \
 *   npx ts-node scripts/seed-neighborhoods.ts --yes
 *
 * Refuses to run without --yes or against an emulator env — same guards as
 * every other seed script in this directory.
 */
